    "https://ats.talentadore.com/apply/tutkijatohtorin-projektitutkijan-maaraaikainen-tehtava-matematiikka/Z93gE4?lang=en&UTUID=21670": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researcher / Project Researcher Fixed Term Position (Mathematics)",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Researcher / Project Researcher Fixed Term Position (Mathematics) | Department of Mathematics and Statistics JavaScript is disabled. Please enable JavaScript for the best recruiting experience. Apply for this position Postdoctoral Researcher / Project Researcher Fixed Term Position (Mathematics) The number theory research group at University of Turku is seeking to employ a talented postdoctoral researcher or a project researcher (about to obtain her/his PhD degree soon) to work on analytic number theory for the period 1.1.2027-31.12.2028. The fixed-term position is expected to start on 1 January 2027 or by agreement. A researcher will work in projects funded by Simons Foundation as part of the number theory research group and Finnish Centre of Excellence in Randomness and Structures. Job description The primary task of the researcher is conducting high-quality scientific research. The members of the researcher group are able to work on research topics from their own research plans together with their international contacts. Who we are looking for Applicants are required to have a PhD degree in mathematics or to complete a PhD degree soon (project researcher), preferably on analytic number theory, and to be able to conduct independent research. Only applicants whose research plan concerns analytic number theory are considered. The most important selection criteria are the scientific merits of the candidate and the quality of the research plan. Preference will be given to those candidates whose research interests lie in multiplicative or additive number theory, L-functions or in the interface between additive combinatorics and analytic number theory. The qualification requirements of the positions are determined in the University of Turku rules of procedure . Accordingly, requirements for a postdoctoral researcher are a doctoral degree and the ability to do independent scientific work as well as having the necessary teaching skills. In case a person selected for a project researcher position does not have a doctoral degree in the beginning of employment, the title will be a project researcher. A project researcher is required to have a higher university degree. When assessing the merits of the applicants, special emphasis will place on competence and practical expertise in the field in question. Benefits We offer you responsible and interesting tasks and the opportunity to develop your professional skills in a versatile operating environment. You get a professional and inspiring team to support your work. We take care of your well-being at work and the functionality of your everyday life, e.g. with the help of flexible working hours and our well-being services.Please read more about University of Turku as an employer from our Come work with us! pages. The European Commission has awarded the University of Turku the right to use the HR Excellence in Research quality label . The label is a token of the University's commitment to continuous development of the position and working conditions of researchers according to the guidelines set forth in the European Charter for Researchers. The university offers good support and orientation for international hires. Please learn more about the Finnish culture and relocation to Finland: City of Turku Welcome visitor International House of Turku Career in Southwestern Finland (with information on Turku) Guide to Finland: infoFinland.fi This is Finland Finland - a superpower of education and innovations | University of Turku (utu.fi) Salary & trial period The salary is determined in accordance with the university salary system for teaching and research personnel and will depend on the degree and qualifications of the applicant. For a postdoctoral researcher (levels 5-6), the monthly salary will be in the beginning of the employment on average 3700–4600 euros/month, depending on previous experience and skills, and being 3700 € in the beginning of an employment typically. For a project researcher (levels 2-4), the salary will be in the beginning of the employment on average 2550-3400 euros/month, depending on previous experience and skills, and being. The amount of the salary is defined when the employment contract is prepared. A six (6) month trial period applies to the position. How to apply and further information Submit your application through our electronic recruitment system by Tuesday 20th of October 2026 at 4:00 p.m. local time in Finland (Europe/Helsinki) . The application link can be found on the university’s website at the beginning of the advertisement (\"Apply for this job\"). Applicants should enclose with their application 1) CV 2) motivational letter 3) research plan 4) list of publications and 5) a copy of a PhD degree certificate (or Master Degree certificate in case the applicant does not yet have PhD degree). The application form cannot be saved as a draft. However, after submitting, you can return to edit your application via the link you receive by email. The application can be edited until the application deadline. You have 6 hours to complete your application before the timeout. Additionally, the applicants should ask two reference letter writers to send a reference letter by e-mail to HR Specialist Susanna Virtanen, susanna.virtanen@utu.fi by the application deadline . For further information on the available positions contact Professor Kaisa Matomäki ( kaisa.matomaki@utu.fi ). Apply between and Department of Mathematics and Statistics In the Department of Mathematics and Statistics the main research areas in mathematics and applied mathematics include discrete mathematics, theoretical computer science, number theory, analysis, optimization, mathematical modelling and insurance mathematics. The Center of Statistics is in charge of the research and consulting in statistics within the university. Its key research areas include latent variable models, methods for cohort and efficacy studies, and themes concerning macro and financial econometrics. In the Faculty of Science , we seek the truth and develop solutions for sustainable future and intelligent society. Science Fiction becomes reality. The University of Turku is an inspiring and international academic community of 25,000 students and staff in Southwest Finland. We build a sustainable future with multidisciplinary research, education, and collaboration. With us, your work will have a significant impact and relevance in the changing world. See our open vacancies Homepage LinkedIn Facebook Youtube Instagram Information for the applicant The application form cannot be saved as a draft. However, after submitting you can return to edit your application via the link you receive by email. The application can be edited until the application deadline. You have 6 hours to complete your application before the timeout. Instructions for submitting a job application Apply for this position English Suomi English Postdoctoral Researcher / Project Researcher Fixed Term Position (Mathematics) Add your picture Are you sure you want to withdraw this application? Would you like to tell us the reason for this withdrawal? Back to form Saving changes Saved!"
