    "https://ats.talentadore.com/apply/4-collegium-fellow-positions-tias/8VXKWX?UTUID=21661": {
      "title": "4 Collegium Fellow positions (TIAS)",
      "description": "4 Collegium Fellow positions (TIAS) | Turku Institute for Advanced Studies (TIAS) JavaScript is disabled. Please enable JavaScript for the best recruiting experience. Apply for this position 4 Collegium Fellow positions (TIAS) Turku Institute for Advanced Studies (TIAS) invites applications for four (4) Collegium Fellow (Collegium Researcher) positions for a three-year period starting from 1 September 2027. TIAS Fellows are selected via an international call for applications and TIAS welcomes applications from projects based in any discipline within its five constituent faculties (Economics, Education, Humanities, Law and Social Sciences). Selection of successful applicants will be on the basis of academic excellence. Job description The main task of TIAS Fellows is to carry out an internationally excellent research project over a three year period, during which the results of the project should be disseminated in a number of ways. Fellows are also required to contribute to the intellectual life of the Institute via such things as attending and presenting at TIAS meetings, organising TIAS events and cross disciplinary working with their co-Fellows. The positions are located at one of the campuses of the University of Turku and successful candidates are required to be resident in Finland. In addition to TIAS meetings, Fellows are expected to attend the campus regularly. TIAS Fellows are located in departments which act as hosts to the research. Selected applicants will benefit from being hosted within departments in the University’s faculties, while also being part of the vibrant TIAS research community. Who we are looking for Collegium Fellow is defined as being within twelve (12) years of applicants having passed their PhD. Tenured Professors (i.e. those with the title of Professor) are not eligible to apply. Successful publishing and other scientific work as well as significant activity and engagement in international academic networks after gaining the doctorate are requirements for appointment to a Collegium Fellow post. Applicants are expected to have ambitious research plans that aim at new scientific breakthroughs. TIAS supports the research priorities of the University of Turku and applicants should identify both the department within which they wish to be located and outline relevant areas of the department’s research interests which align with their own. Applicants must also outline how their work relates to one or more of the multidisciplinary themes and areas of strength of the University of Turku and why they particularly wish to be part of the TIAS community. Selection of successful applicants will be on the basis of academic excellence. External Reviewers are asked to rank, from 1–6, the following: (i) applicants’ previous academic achievements relative to their career stage, (ii) quality of the research plan and feasibility of the research given the three years’ time limit, (iii) theoretical and methodological framework of the research, (iv) evaluation of the proposed publications and outputs, and (v) an overall assessment. Reviewers are also asked to comment on any ethical issues around the proposed research. Based on the external evaluations, the TIAS Board of Management makes final decisions on the successful applicants. Benefits TIAS is a research collegium which supports the bottom-up development of excellent early- and mid- career stage academics through the provision of three years of funding, enabling them to carry out self-designed research projects. TIAS Fellows have limited work obligations beyond conducting research. All TIAS Fellows have the opportunity to contribute to teaching activities at the University of Turku. Such contributions will make up a maximum of 5 % of a Fellow’s annual work load of 1612 hours. In addition, they may devote another 5 % of their total working time to other academic and administration duties. Please read more about University of Turku as an employer from our Come work with us! pages. The European Commission has awarded the University of Turku the right to use the HR Excellence in Research quality label . The label is a token of the University's commitment to continuous development of the position and working conditions of researchers according to the guidelines set forth in the European Charter for Researchers. The university offers good support and orientation for international hires. Please learn more about the Finnish culture and relocation to Finland: City of Turku Welcome visitor International House of Turku Working culture: infoFinland.fi This is Finland Careers in Southwest Finland Finland - a superpower of education and innovations | University of Turku (utu.fi) The University of Turku is among the top of the world’s universities in most rankings and among the best universities in the world in certain fields. Our high-quality basic research, a multidisciplinary research profile and close cooperation in research infrastructures creates the basis for international top research. Read more about University of Turku in international university rankings. The University of Turku has several high-quality research infrastructures required for cutting-edge research. Learn more about the roadmap of research infrastructures and how the research infrastructure and expert teams offer tailored solutions for businesses and organisations . Salary and trial period TIAS Fellows’ salaries are determined in accordance with the university salary system for teaching and research personnel.  The salary for Collegium Researcher positions corresponds to a requirement level 7 and the pre-estimated personal performance percentage of 17% (current gross salary 5 295 €/month). Progress in the researcher's personal performance can be taken into account when determining the salary during employment. The position has a trial period of six months. How to apply Please read first carefully the detailed instructions and guidance for applicants including information about the required application documents. Please submit your application through our online recruitment system. The closing date for applications is 13 November 2026 (16:00 Finnish time, GMT/UTC +2). Further information For more information on TIAS please see the TIAS website . An information session for applicants will be held online on Monday 28 September 2026 between 14.00 and 16.00 Finnish time (GMT/UTC +3). Please note that the information session covers both TIAS Call for Postdoctoral and Collegium Fellow positions , and TIES2 MSCA COFUND Fellowship Call . The TIAS Director will introduce the Calls, explain the applications and reviews process and answer questions. A recording/Powerpoint slides of this will be placed online. Please sign up to the information session in order to get the online meeting link. Further questions about the Call may also be addressed to tias@utu.fi . Apply between and Turku Institute for Advanced Studies (TIAS) Turku Institute for Advanced Studies (TIAS) promotes cutting-edge university research in humanities and social sciences. It is a joint enterprise between the faculties of Humanities, Education, Social Sciences and Law and Turku School of Economics, founded in 2008. TIAS aims to establish a community of interdisciplinary researchers dedicated to research excellence. The University of Turku is an inspiring and international academic community of 25,000 students and staff in Southwest Finland. We build a sustainable future with multidisciplinary research, education, and collaboration. With us, your work will have a significant impact and relevance in the changing world. See our open vacancies Homepage LinkedIn Facebook X Youtube Instagram Phone: +358 29 450 5000 Email: tias@utu.fi Location: 20014 Turun yliopisto Apply for this position English Suomi English 4 Collegium Fellow positions (TIAS) Add your picture Are you sure you want to withdraw this application? Would you like to tell us the reason for this withdrawal? Back to form Saving changes Saved!"
    },
    "https://ats.talentadore.com/apply/projektitutkija-vaitoskirjatutkija/ZvnVxQ?lang=en&UTUID=21658": {
      "title": "Project Researcher/ Doctoral Researcher",
      "description": "Project Researcher/ Doctoral Researcher | Department of Psychology and Speech-Language Pathology JavaScript is disabled. Please enable JavaScript for the best recruiting experience. Apply for this position Project Researcher/ Doctoral Researcher At the Department of Psychology and Speech-Language Pathology in the Faculty of Social Sciences at the University of Turku, a fixed-term position as a Project Researcher/Doctoral Researcher is open for applications for the period January 1, 2027–August 31, 2030. The employment will begin on January 1, 2027, or as agreed. The application period opens on September 18, 2026 and closes on October 16, 2026 at 4:00 p.m. (Europe/Helsinki). The recruited researcher will participate in a project funded by Research Council of Finland and led by Professor Minna Lehtonen. The project investigates the relationship between bilingual language use, language switching in particular, and executive functions. A central aim of the project is to determine whether the role of executive functions changes as language proficiency develops and how such learning modifies brain structure and function. The research is also related to the question of whether bilingualism or second language learning can be expected to show cognitive or brain-health benefits beyond language proficiency itself. The project involves international collaboration with, e.g., the University of Barcelona. The doctoral researcher will be supervised by Professor Minna Lehtonen and Postdoctoral Researcher Sini Hämäläinen. Job description The Project Researcher/Doctoral Researcher will investigate automatization of foreign-language use using behavioural methods and the functional and structural brain changes associated with these processes using TMS and MRI/DTI methods. The selected candidate will gain diverse methodological experience through the project and have the opportunity to become familiar with research in psycholinguistics, cognitive psychology, and neuroscience. The appointed researcher will participate in the design and implementation of studies, data collection and analysis, and the scientific reporting and publication of research findings as part of their doctoral dissertation work. Who we are looking for Requirements The position of Project Researcher/Doctoral Researcher is intended for an early‑career researcher who has not yet completed a doctoral degree. The eligibility requirements for the positions of Project Researcher and Doctoral Researcher are laid down in the University-of-turku-rules-of-procedure.pdf . Applicants must hold a relevant Master’s degree, for example in psychology, speech‑language pathology, or cognitive neuroscience. The eligibility requirements for the position must be fulfulled by the end of the application period for the position. For the position of Doctoral Researcher, applicants must have the right to pursue a doctoral degree at the University of Turku and a research plan for a doctoral dissertation that aligns with the project’s topic. If the selected applicant does not have the right to pursue a doctoral degree at the University of Turku by the end of the application period, the position will initially be filled under the title Project Researcher . The selected person will then be expected to apply for the right to pursue doctoral studies in the next possible application round. For additional information, please see University of Turku Graduate School (UTUGS) and Doctoral Programmes . In exceptional cases, we may also consider applicants who have completed nearly all the studies required for a Master's degree in a relevant field. In such cases, the job title at the start of the employment will be Research Assistant . In addition, the successful candidate is expected to have: Experience in research on language processing, cognitive neuroscience, or bilingualism, or a strong interest in these areas Experience with statistical analysis methods and processing of research data Knowledge of TMS and MRI/DTI research methods, or willingness to acquire such expertise Ability to work independently as well as collaboratively in a multidisciplinary research team Strong interpersonal and communication skills Excellent written and spoken English skills The following will be considered an advantage: Programming and data analysis skills (e.g. R, Python, or equivalent tools) Good written and spoken Finnish skills The primary place of work is Turku, and the selected candidates must reside in Finland for the duration of the employment. We value collegiality and promote equality, diversity, and inclusivity. We encourage all qualified applicants with different backgrounds to apply for our open positions. Benefits We offer you responsible and interesting work tasks, as well as the opportunity to develop your professional skills in a diverse working environment. You will be supported by a skilled and inspiring team. We take care of your well‑being at work and the smoothness of your everyday life through, for example, flexible working hours and our well‑being services. Read more about us on our Welcome to work with us - page , where you can find additional information about what the University offers its employees. The European Commission has awarded the University of Turku the right to use the HR Excellence in Research logo . The logo is a token of the University's commitment to continuous development of the position and working conditions of researchers according to the guidelines set forth in the European Charter for Researchers. The university offers good support and orientation for international hires. Please learn more about the Finnish culture and relocation to Finland: City of Turku Welcome visitor International House of Turku Working culture: infoFinland.fi This is Finland Careers in Southwest Finland Finland - a superpower of education and innovations | University of Turku (utu.fi) The University of Turku is among the top of the world’s universities in most rankings and among the best universities in the world in certain fields. Our high-quality basic research, a multidisciplinary research profile and close cooperation in research infrastructures creates the basis for international top research. Read more about University of Turku in international university rankings. The University of Turku has several high-quality research infrastructures required for cutting-edge research. Learn more about the roadmap of research infrastructures and how the research infrastructure and expert teams offer tailored solutions for businesses and organizations . Salary and trial period The salary is determined by the collective agreement system of Finnish universities. The position belongs to the category of teaching and research personnel. The pre-estimated salary will be in average (OV02-OV04)   2 565-3 460 eur/month. The exact salary will depend on the person’s competence and research experience and will be specified when the employment contract is prepared. Should the successful candidate initially start in the position of Research Assistant, the starting salary (OV1) is on average 2460 euros/month, depending on competence and experience. The position has a trial period of six (6) months. How to apply Please submit your application through our online recruitment system.  Applications must be submitted by October 16, 2026 at 16.00 p.m. (Europe / Helsinki time zone). Applicants must attach the following documents to their application: Curriculum vitae (CV) List of publications, if you have publications Motivation letter. Please specify research interests and experiences; one page is sufficient. Possible other documents that may affect the decision-making Please, attach all the above-mentioned documents to your application. The documents are essential in assessing the applications . The appendices should follow the guidelines of the faculty. Candidates selected for interview will be notified in week 43 and the interviews will be held in week 45. Further information For further information about the position, please contact Professor Minna Lehtonen, mihleh@utu.fi . For more information about the recruitment process, please contact HR specialist Nina Kramsu, tel. +358 29 450 4981, nikram@utu.fi . Apply between and Department of Psychology and Speech-Language Pathology The Department of Psychology and Speech-Language Pathology conducts internationally high-quality research and provides research-based undergraduate and graduate education in the subjects of psychology and speech-language pathology. The location of the department in the Faculty of Social Sciences in the vicinity of Turku University Central Hospital enables diverse interdisciplinary scientific activities. In addition to teaching and research, the department also acts as a significant influencer in the field of speech-language pathology and psychology. The aim of the department is to reach the international top in research and teaching of speech therapy and psychology. The Faculty of Social Sciences is a vibrant scientific community of two thousand academic individuals. The faculty's disciplines provide a diverse and complementary picture of society. In the core is society and analysis of its functioning. The University of Turku is an inspiring and international academic community of 25,000 students and staff in Southwest Finland. We build a sustainable future with multidisciplinary research, education, and collaboration. With us, your work will have a significant impact and relevance in the changing world. See our open vacancies Homepage LinkedIn Facebook Youtube Instagram Phone: +358504726762 Email: nina.kramsu@utu.fi Location: Turku Information for the applicant The application form cannot be saved as a draft. However, after submitting you can return to edit your application via the link you receive by email. The application can be edited until the application deadline. You have 6 hours to complete your application before the timeout. Instructions for submitting a job application Apply for this position English Suomi English Project Researcher/ Doctoral Researcher Add your picture Are you sure you want to withdraw this application? Would you like to tell us the reason for this withdrawal? Back to form Saving changes Saved!"
    },
    "https://ats.talentadore.com/apply/projektitutkijan-vaitoskirjatutkijan-tehtava-metsaluonnon-monimuotoisuutta-valuma-alueella-tutkivaan-hankkeeseen/DokY3j?lang=en&UTUID=21690": {
      "title": "Project Researcher / Doctoral Researcher Position in a Project on Forest Biodiversity",
      "description": "Project Researcher / Doctoral Researcher Position in a Project on Forest Biodiversity at the Catchment Scale | Department of Geography and Geology JavaScript is disabled. Please enable JavaScript for the best recruiting experience. Apply for this position Project Researcher / Doctoral Researcher Position in a Project on Forest Biodiversity at the Catchment Scale The Department of Geography and Geology at the Faculty of Science, University of Turku, invites applications for a fixed-term Project Researcher / Doctoral Researcher position (48 months), starting no earlier than 1 November 2026 , or as agreed. The Project Researcher / Doctoral Researcher will work within the Towards more Biodiverse and Efficient Logging and Defence Operations (BiodiLogDef) project funded by Business Finland and the Digital Waters Flagship (DIWA) . Within the BiodiLogDef project, the research will focus particularly on developing indicators of forest biodiversity using novel remote sensing methods. Within the Digital Waters Flagship, the research will investigate the effects of forest biodiversity on the hydrological cycle at the catchment scale. The position will be based at the Department of Geography and Geology as part of the BiodiLogDef project and the Digital Waters (DIWA) Flagship (digitalwaters.fi). In the BiodiLogDef project, the work is carried out in close collaboration with the Departments of Biology (Prof. Toni Laaksonen) and Biodiversity Sciences (Prof. Ilari Sääksjärvi). Job description The successful candidate will work particularly on the following research themes: Development of indicators describing forest biodiversity Processing and management of remote sensing data, particularly lidar datasets The role of vegetation cover in the hydrological cycle at the catchment scale Who we are looking for The position is intended for an early-career researcher who has not yet completed a doctoral degree. Eligibility requirements for Project Researchers and Doctoral Researchers are defined in the Regulations of the University of Turku. We expect applicants to have: A suitable Master's degree (e.g. in natural sciences, engineering, data science, or a related field). The degree must be completed by the end of the application period. Ability to work collaboratively in a multidisciplinary research team. Competence in applying statistical methods and modelling. Experience in handling large geospatial and remote sensing datasets in environmental or natural sciences. Excellent written and oral communication skills in English. The following qualifications will be considered an advantage: Strong IT and programming skills (e.g. Python, R). Proficiency in Finnish. Experience in similar research projects. Candidates appointed as Doctoral Researchers must hold the right to pursue a doctoral degree at the University of Turku and have a doctoral research plan that aligns with the project topic. If the selected candidate does not hold doctoral study rights at the University of Turku by the end of the application period, the position will initially be filled under the title Project Researcher . The selected candidate will then be expected to apply for doctoral study rights in the next available call for doctoral admissions. More information is available through the University of Turku Graduate School (UTUGS) Join us for your doctoral studies at the University of Turku! | University of Turku and its doctoral programmes. We value collegiality and promote equality, diversity, and inclusivity. We encourage all qualified applicants with different backgrounds to apply for our open positions. Benefits We offer you responsible and interesting tasks and the opportunity to develop your professional skills in a versatile operating environment. You get a professional and inspiring team to support your work. We take care of your well-being at work and the functionality of your everyday life, e.g. with the help of flexible working hours and our well-being services. Possibilities to develop your expertise – We encourage our personnel to develop their professional expertise by offering versatile training and competence development possibilities which employees can take advantage of during their working hours. Also, the course offering of Open University is free of charge for our personnel. Your well-being is important to us! – In addition to comprehensive occupational health care, our own well-being services monitor, support and develop the well-being of our personnel. You are entitled to use the CampusSport’s services at a personnel price. We support your work-life balance – Flexible working hours and extensive remote work options help you balance work and leisure time. An inspiring and supportive work community – We encourage each other and value working together! Please read more about University of Turku as an employer from our Come work with us! pages. The European Commission has awarded the University of Turku the right to use the HR Excellence in Research quality label . The label is a token of the University's commitment to continuous development of the position and working conditions of researchers according to the guidelines set forth in the European Charter for Researchers. The university offers good support and orientation for international hires. Please learn more about the Finnish culture and relocation to Finland: City of Turku Welcome visitor International House of Turku Working culture: infoFinland.fi This is Finland Careers in Southwest Finland Finland - a superpower of education and innovations | University of Turku (utu.fi) Salary and trial period The salary is determined in accordance with the university salary system for teaching and research personnel. The job requirement level of the position is 2 – 4.  In addition, a salary component based on personal work performance is paid. Salary, based on previous experience and skills, is approximately 2658 -3300 euros/month at the beginning of the assignment. The position has a trial period of six months. How to apply Please submit your application through our online recruitment system. The closing date for applications is Friday 23.10.2026 at 16.00 (Europe/Helsinki) . Applicants should enclose with their application: A motivation letter (maximum one page) Curriculum vitae (CV) Degree certificates Any other documents relevant to the evaluation of the application Further information For further information about the position, please contact: Associate Professor Ville Kankare, ville.kankare(at)utu.fi With questions about the application process, please contact: HR-specialist Kaisa Ketomäki, kaisa.ketomaki(at)utu.fi Apply between and Department of Geography and Geology The Department of Geography and Geology is an active and versatile unit which studies the Earth and its dynamic natural and anthropogenic phenomena. We conduct research on several continents and our international collaboration is diverse. We use modern research methodologies and state-of-the-art equipment both in the field and in the laboratory. In the Faculty of Science , we seek the truth and develop solutions for sustainable future and intelligent society. Science Fiction becomes reality. The University of Turku is an inspiring and international academic community of 25,000 students and staff in Southwest Finland. We build a sustainable future with multidisciplinary research, education, and collaboration. With us, your work will have a significant impact and relevance in the changing world. See our open vacancies Homepage LinkedIn Facebook Youtube Instagram Information for the applicant The application form cannot be saved as a draft. However, after submitting you can return to edit your application via the link you receive by email. The application can be edited until the application deadline. You have 6 hours to complete your application before the timeout. Instructions for submitting a job application Apply for this position English Suomi English Project Researcher / Doctoral Researcher Position in a Project on Forest Biodiversity at the Catchment Scale Add your picture Are you sure you want to withdraw this application? Would you like to tell us the reason for this withdrawal? Back to form Saving changes Saved!"
    },
    "https://ats.talentadore.com/apply/tutkijatohtorin-erikoistutkijan-maaraaikainen-tehtava-suomen-eso-keskuksella/ZjaYnE?lang=en&UTUID=21694": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral researcher / Senior researcher fixed term position",
      "description": "Postdoctoral researcher / Senior researcher fixed term position at the Finnish Centre for Astronomy with ESO | Finnish Center for Astronomy with ESO JavaScript is disabled. Please enable JavaScript for the best recruiting experience. Apply for this position Postdoctoral researcher / Senior researcher fixed term position at the Finnish Centre for Astronomy with ESO Finnish Centre for Astronomy with ESO (FINCA) invites applications for a three-year postdoctoral/senior researcher position. The starting date is negotiable, but no later than 1st September 2027. The Finnish Centre for Astronomy with ESO (FINCA) is a national research institute that takes care of Finnish co-operation with the European Southern Observatory (ESO), practices and co-ordinates high quality astronomical research, and technological development work related to ESO; participates in researcher training; and promotes co-operation of Finnish universities in astronomy. The ERC-funded BlackHolistic project seeks to create colour movies of black holes and study their astrophysics across scales. The multinational BlackHolistic team is currently building the first single dish mm-wave radio telescope in Africa, the Africa Millimetre Telescope (AMT), which will join the Event Horizon Telescope as well as carry out single dish science. At FINCA BlackHolistic is run jointly by Dr. Elina Lindfors and Dr. Talvikki Hovatta. Job description The research concentrates on the physics of relativistic jets launched from accreting supermassive black holes in active galactic nuclei (AGN). These black hole powered jets are among the most energetic long-lived phenomena in the Universe and despite their ubiquity, many of the fundamental questions regarding their physics are still open. We do not for example understand well their launching and acceleration mechanisms. Your task will be to develop tools and pipelines to statistically compare astronomical observables (e.g. light curves) from numerical simulations against new multi-messenger observations. BlackHolistic is an international research project and you will work closely with the research group of Prof. Sera Markoff (University of Cambridge & University of Amsterdam). The Finnish Group has several PhD students and postdocs and an active environment both at University of Turku and Aalto University Metsähovi Radio Observatory. You will be formally employed by University of Turku, but can choose between UTU and Metsähovi Radio Observatory as your primary work site. Requirements PhD in astronomy, astrophysics or physics (Postdoctoral researcher). Higher university degree (Senior Researcher) if you are in the final stages of your PhD. Strong background in radiative processes and scientific computing Experience in astronomical multi-messenger observations and data analysis A track record of scientific publications in high-quality peer reviewed journals Professional-level communication and presentation skills in English Self-motivated and able to work independently The qualification requirements of the position are stated in the University of Turku Rules of Procedure: https://www.utu.fi/en/university/organisation . Benefits We offer you responsible and interesting tasks and the opportunity to develop your professional skills in a versatile operating environment. You get a professional and inspiring team to support your work. We take care of your well-being at work and the functionality of your everyday life, e.g. with the help of flexible working hours and our well-being services. Possibilities to develop your expertise – We encourage our personnel to develop their professional expertise by offering versatile training and competence development possibilities which employees can take advantage of during their working hours. Also, the course offering of Open University is free of charge for our personnel. Your well-being is important to us! – In addition to comprehensive occupational health care, our own well-being services monitor, support and develop the well-being of our personnel. You are entitled to use the CampusSport’s services at a personnel price. An inspiring and supportive work community – We encourage each other and value working together! Please read more about University of Turku as an employee from our Come work with us! pages. The European Commission has awarded the University of Turku the right to use the HR Excellence in Research quality label . The label is a token of the University's commitment to continuous development of the position and working conditions of researchers according to the guidelines set forth in the European Charter for Researchers. The university offers good support and orientation for international hires. Please learn more about the Finnish culture and relocation to Finland: City of Turku Welcome visitor International House of Turku Working culture: infoFinland.fi This is Finland Careers in Southwest Finland Finland - a superpower of education and innovations | University of Turku (utu.fi) The University of Turku is among the top of the world’s universities in most rankings and among the best universities in the world in certain fields. Our high-quality basic research, a multidisciplinary research profile and close cooperation in research infrastructures creates the basis for international top research. Read more about University of Turku in international university rankings. The University of Turku has several high-quality research infrastructures required for cutting-edge research. Learn more about the roadmap of research infrastructures and how the research infrastructure and expert teams offer tailored solutions for businesses and organizations . Salary and trial period The selected candidate should start in the position by September 1st 2027 the latest. The fixed-term contract is for three years. The salary is determined by the collective agreement system of Finnish universities, aligning with the teaching and research personnel category. The salary for a Postdoctoral researcher or Senior researcher is based on levels 5-6. A personal performance component is added to the task-specific salary. The starting salary for the position is approximately 3600-3800 €/month. The amount of the salary is defined when the employment contract is prepared and is influenced by previous experience and skills. Support for participation in conferences and research visits is available. The position has a trial period of six (6) months. How to apply Applications must be submitted by 6 November 2026 (16:00 EET) at the latest via the electronic application form of the University of Turku but we will start reviewing and interviewing candidates immediately. However, all applications received by the deadline will be reviewed and the decision will be made after the application period has ended. This job announcement can be found from the University of Turku recruitment page: http://www.utu.fi/careers . Applications in English must include: a CV a list of relevant publications a motivation letter (max. 2 pages) degree certificates At least two letters of recommendation must be arranged to be sent directly to Saija Marjasto, saija.marjasto(at)utu.fi. We value collegiality and promote equality, diversity, and inclusivity. We encourage all qualified applicants with different backgrounds to apply for our open positions. Further information For more information on the position, contact Dr. Talvikki Hovatta, talvikki.hovatta(at)utu.fi or Dr. Elina Lindfors, elilin(at)utu.fi. For more information on the application process, contact HR Specialist Saija Marjasto, saija.marjasto(at)utu.fi. Apply between and Finnish Center for Astronomy with ESO FINCA - Finnish Centre for Astronomy with ESO practises and co-ordinates Finnish high quality research in fields of astronomy with European Southern Observatory (ESO) and promotes technological development work related to ESO. The University of Turku is an inspiring and international academic community of 25,000 students and staff in Southwest Finland. We build a sustainable future with multidisciplinary research, education, and collaboration. With us, your work will have a significant impact and relevance in the changing world. See our open vacancies Homepage LinkedIn Facebook Youtube Instagram Location: Vesilinnantie 5 Information for the applicant The application form cannot be saved as a draft. However, after submitting you can return to edit your application via the link you receive by email. The application can be edited until the application deadline. You have 6 hours to complete your application before the timeout. Instructions for submitting a job application Apply for this position English Suomi English Postdoctoral researcher / Senior researcher fixed term position at the Finnish Centre for Astronomy with ESO Add your picture Are you sure you want to withdraw this application? Would you like to tell us the reason for this withdrawal? Back to form Saving changes Saved!"
    },
    "https://ats.talentadore.com/apply/doctoral-researcher-position-in-msca-doctoral-network/Dokgyj?UTUID=21687": {
      "title": "DOCTORAL RESEARCHER position in MSCA Doctoral Network",
      "description": "DOCTORAL RESEARCHER position in MSCA Doctoral Network  | Turku PET Centre JavaScript is disabled. Please enable JavaScript for the best recruiting experience. Apply for this position DOCTORAL RESEARCHER position in MSCA Doctoral Network Marie Skłodowska Curie (MSCA) Doctoral Networks (MSCA-DN) Applications are invited for 1 full-time Doctoral Researcher position at the Turku PET Centre, University of Turku, Finland. PhD PROJECT - Effect of ischemic heart disease on multiorgan perfusion Type of contract: Fixed-term Duration: Three years (36 months), starting 1.4.2027 or as agreed Job Status: Full-time A highly innovative system, called long axial field of view (LAFOV) PET/CT, has become available and is the ideal medical imaging modality to study diseases and molecular processes at the whole body/systems biology level with multiple radiotracers. Studying diseases and diagnosing patients using PET/CT imaging should use a whole body/systems biology approach, i.e., a comprehensive whole-body characterization of disease, and it should be longitudinal and should use multiple radiotracers. However, LAFOV PET/CT is so new that we lack the necessary tools, methodologies, imaging procedures and skilled scientists to effectively address key applications in patient care and research. With the PREFERENCE project we aim to develop innovative LAFOV PET/CT methodologies to perform and support ground-breaking new clinical research. PREFERENCE will train the next generation of researchers specialized in LAFOV PET/CT who will capitalize on the new clinical and research opportunities of the LAFOV PET/CT system. By performing research in both academia and industrial groups, researchers within PREFERENCE receive training in a unique combination of (soft) skills across disciplines and sectors. PREFERENCE will develop new LAFOV PET/CT methodologies, and perform LAFOV PET/CT clinical studies across disease areas to obtain novel biological insights. This project was selected by the EU as worthy of funding under the HE Marie Sklodowska Curie Action. The consortium consists of 12 academic partners with a strong expertise in quantitative (LAFOV) PET/CT imaging as well as industrial partners developing imaging equipment or providing multi-center image analysis solutions and services. Description of the advertised position (DC 9) This is a 3-y full time position as an doctoral candidate (DC) under the auspice of the MSCA DN programme. The overall arching goal is to conduct hands-on LAFOV PET/CT clinical research aiming to increase the clinical applicability of LAFOV PET/CT in patient care while gaining new insights and knowledge regarding the pathophysiology of diseases. You will develop and evaluate methods how LAFOV PET/CT enables to measure perfusion simultaneously in all organs during a routine examination of myocardial perfusion. In addition, there is poissibility to expand your expertise to cardiovascular inflammation using a novel inflammatory tracer, 18-F-folate. You will investigate the systemic impact of atherosclerosis and myocardial ischemia due to coronary artery disease (CAD) on other organs and how these are linked to the sensations and experiences of the patient. During your secondments to Regionhospitalet in Copenhagen, the University of Edinburgh and Siemens Healthineers, you will develop and evaluate methods evaluate methods for automated analysis for LAFOV perfusion studies, perform multi-organ multiparametric kinetic analysis and implement and evaluate parametric LAFOV imaging with reconstruction tools. Further, the project may include short-term visits to different PREFERENCE partners for data and software exchange. General eligibility criteria Mobility Rule: The fellow may not have resided in the country where the research training activities take place for more than 12 months in the 3 years immediately prior to the recruitment date (and not have carried out their main activity (work, studies, etc.) in that country). Doctoral candidate: The fellow must be — at the date of recruitment — an ‘ doctoral candidate ’ (i.e. not have a doctoral degree). Special requirements Successfully completed studies in Medical Physics, Biomedical Engineering, Medicine and Health Biosciences (MSc degree or equivalent) Very good command of the English language (additional skills in Finnish will be of benefit) Good communication skills (a pre-requisite for cooperating in a multi-disciplinary environment) Willingness to travel and flexibility Technical skills will be of benefit Prior experience with medical imaging data will be of benefit Appropriate physical condition to work in a radiation protection control area Right to pursue a doctoral degree The selected candidate must obtain the right to pursue a doctoral degree at the Faculty of Medicine and be approved by the Doctoral Programme of Clinical Research (DPCR) before the employment can be confirmed, unless the applicant already holds a valid doctoral study right. Benefits We offer you responsible and interesting tasks and the opportunity to develop your professional skills in a versatile operating environment. You get a professional and inspiring team to support your work. We take care of your well-being at work and the functionality of your everyday life, e.g. with the help of flexible working hours and our well-being services. Possibilities to develop your expertise – We encourage our personnel to develop their professional expertise by offering versatile training and competence development possibilities which employees can take advantage of during their working hours. Also, the course offering of Open University is free of charge for our personnel. Your well-being is important to us! – In addition to comprehensive occupational health care, our own well-being services monitor, support and develop the well-being of our personnel. You are entitled to use the CampusSport’s services at a personnel price. We support your work-life balance – Flexible working hours and extensive remote work options help you balance work and leisure time. An inspiring and supportive work community – We encourage each other and value working together! Please read more about University of Turku as an employer from our Come work with us! pages. The European Commission has awarded the University of Turku the right to use the HR Excellence in Research quality label . The label is a token of the University's commitment to continuous development of the position and working conditions of researchers according to the guidelines set forth in the European Charter for Researchers. The university offers good support and orientation for international hires. Please learn more about the Finnish culture and relocation to Finland: City of Turku Welcome visitor infoFinland.fi International House of Turku Working culture: infoFinland.fi This is Finland Careers in Southwest Finland Finland - a superpower of education and innovations | University of Turku (utu.fi) The University of Turku is among the top of the world’s universities in most rankings and among the best universities in the world in certain fields. Our high-quality basic research, a multidisciplinary research profile and close cooperation in research infrastructures creates the basis for international top research. Read more about University of Turku in international university rankings. The University of Turku has several high-quality research infrastructures required for cutting-edge research. Learn more about the roadmap of research infrastructures and how the research infrastructure and expert teams offer tailored solutions for businesses and organizations . Salary and trial period You will be appointed as fulltime PhD candidate for 3 years. The successful candidate will receive a salary in accordance with the Marie Skłodowska-Curie Actions, that includes a gross living allowance of 4010 EUR/month (correction factor to be applied for Finland), a monthly mobility allowance of 710 EUR and depending on your familiar status, a family monthly allowance of 660 EUR. Please note that these amounts include taxes and compulsory employer contributions that will be deducted to make the net salary. The exact net salary will be confirmed upon appointment. The total salary is about 3500 EUR per month in the beginning and may increase with improved expertise. Note: The monthly gross salary may vary somewhat in different years, as side costs change. The position has a trial period of six months. How to apply Please submit your application through our online recruitment system. The closing date for applications is 30 November, 2026 at 16.00 EEST. Please write your application and accompanying documents in English. Full applications should include A motivation letter A Europass CV (https://europass.cedefop.europa.eu/documents/curriculum-vitae) Copies of your relevant certificates Contact details of two references Further information PREFERENCE: https://preference-consortium.eu/ Turku PET Centre: Home - Turku PET Centre Recruitment process After assessing compliance with the mobility rule and eligibility for the position based on your CV and motivation letter you might be invited for several online or in-person interviews. Selection of the candidates and invitation for the interviews will be done by the local (host) supervisory team. These interviews will be performed by the local (host) supervisory team as well as an international scientific mentor from the network and, possibly, one of the scientific advisors. Information on your application will be shared with the coordinator of the consortium for centralized coordination and registration of the recruitment process. Information on the exact employment conditions will be provided by the host institution and can also be found on their job announcement board, information on salary (gross and net salary, social security benefits etc) will be communicated during the interview and upon appointment by the host institution. Apply between and Turku PET Centre The National PET Centre is a joint institution of University of Turku, Åbo Akademi University and Turku University hospital, which is concentrated in research of positron emission tomography and offers imaging services for example to academic research, clinical diagnostics, and drug development. The University of Turku is an inspiring and international academic community of 25,000 students and staff in Southwest Finland. We build a sustainable future with multidisciplinary research, education, and collaboration. With us, your work will have a significant impact and relevance in the changing world. See our open vacancies Homepage LinkedIn Facebook Youtube Instagram Information for the applicant The application form cannot be saved as a draft. However, after submitting you can return to edit your application via the link you receive by email. The application can be edited until the application deadline. You have 6 hours to complete your application before the timeout. Instructions for submitting a job application Apply for this position DOCTORAL RESEARCHER position in MSCA Doctoral Network Add your picture Are you sure you want to withdraw this application? Would you like to tell us the reason for this withdrawal? Back to form Saving changes Saved!"
    },
    "https://ats.talentadore.com/apply/1-2-doctoral-researchers-in-human-centered-world-model-for-human-robot-interaction/8R2LY0?UTUID=21695": {
      "title": "1-2 Doctoral Researchers in Human-Centered World Model for Human-Robot Interaction",
      "description": "1-2 Doctoral Researchers in Human-Centered World Model for Human-Robot Interaction | Department of Computing JavaScript is disabled. Please enable JavaScript for the best recruiting experience. Apply for this position 1-2 Doctoral Researchers in Human-Centered World Model for Human-Robot Interaction The Department of Computing is looking for one to two Doctoral Researchers to join a research group of ELLIS PI, Associate Professor Xucong Zhang. You will be working alongside colleagues from academia, ELLIS Institute Finland community and industry. The fixed-term employment starts in November 2026 (or by mutual agreement) and the length of the position is four years (48 months). The research group fosters a collaborative and innovative environment with ELLIS Institute Finland and University of Turku, pushing the boundaries of AI and Foundation Model research with a strong emphasis on real-world impact. Our work bridges technical sophistication with real-world applications, exploring fundamental research questions in multiple human interactive behavior modeling, understanding, and generation, with the aim of natural human-AI interaction. We aim to build a world-model containing multiple virtual human avatars interaction for large-scale training data generation, insert the social aspect of interaction, and train the interactive model to drive the intelligent agent. ELLIS Institute Finland ( https://www.ellisinstitute.fi ) is a newly established world-class research hub in AI and machine learning. We are developing an ecosystem of top talents, businesses and investments in Finland, with fundamental machine learning research at the core. The Institute is part of the European Laboratory for Learning and Intelligent Systems (ELLIS), which aims to build a pan-European institution for machine learning research. Job description We are seeking highly motivated and talented Doctoral Researchers to join our dynamic team. The successful candidates will contribute to cutting-edge research at the intersection of World Model, Human-AI Interaction, and Generative AI. This position offers a unique opportunity to conduct fundamental and applied research on the next generation of AI systems for addressing critical challenges. Research Areas of Focus: The successful candidate(s) will engage in research within one or more of the following areas. Social Intelligence and Human-Centered AI: Investigating and developing social-aware interactions between multiple humans in generative modelling. Multimodal Learning and Representation: Building a system to capture the complex behavior with multimodal including audio, body gesture, eye gaze, and hand pose. Embodied AI and Physical AI Systems: Investigating how complex interactions can be represented, integrated, and learned across diverse domains, modalities, and environments. Responsibilities: Conduct original, high-quality research leading to publications in top-tier conferences and journals. Develop and implement novel algorithms and models in specified research areas. Contribute to the design and execution of research projects, including generative modeling, experimentation, and analysis. Collaborate effectively with interdisciplinary teams, including domain experts, and fellow researchers. Participate in lab meetings, seminars, and other academic activities. Contribute to or assist with teaching activities within related programs. Who we are looking for Requirements MSc degree in Computer Science, Information System, or Artificial Intelligence. A solid foundation in deep learning and 3D modeling. Excellent analytical and problem-solving skills. Excellent communication skills in English (written and spoken). Programming skills (e.g., Python). Interest in collaborative research with both academia and industry. Qualification requirements The eligibility criteria for prospective applicants are defined in the University of Turku Rules of Procedure: university-of-turku-rules-of-procedure.pdf . A person selected for the post of Doctoral Researcher is required to have a right to pursue a doctoral degree at the University of Turku. In addition, when acquiring their degree or otherwise, they are required to have demonstrated the ability to undertake postgraduate studies and the capacity to complete a doctoral degree in accordance with the research plan. Please note that before obtaining the study right for a Doctoral Program, the job title will be Project Researcher , and the employment contract will be made until 31.3.2027. The candidate is expected to apply for the study right in the next available Autumn 2026 call to e.g. the Doctoral Programme in Technology. Thus, please check the student information and application criteria: Doctoral Programme in Technology - Admission Criteria and Instructions for Applicants | University of Turku (please pay attention to the mandatory skill level in English). Read more about the University of Turku's doctoral programmes and how to apply for study rights: Join us for your doctoral studies at the University of Turku! | University of Turku In exceptional cases, we may also consider applicants who have completed nearly all the studies required for a master's degree in a relevant field. In such cases, the job title at the start of the employment will be Research Assistant, and the starting salary (OV1) is on average 2400 euros/month, depending on competence and experience. We value collegiality and promote equality, diversity, and inclusivity. We encourage all qualified applicants with different backgrounds to apply for our open positions. Benefits We offer A four-year fully funded Doctoral Researcher position A stimulating and supportive research environment with access to state-of-the-art computational resources (e.g., GPUs, computing clusters). A dynamic working environment in collaboration with the ELLIS Institute Finland, the University of Turku research group, and other international partners. Opportunities for collaboration with leading researchers in AI, including both academic and industrial partners. Participation in cutting-edge projects with real-world impact on human-AI interaction. Opportunities for professional development, conference attendance, and networking. We offer you responsible and interesting tasks and the opportunity to develop your professional skills in a versatile operating environment. You get a professional and inspiring team to support your work. We take care of your well-being at work and the functionality of your everyday life, e.g. with the help of flexible working hours and our well-being services. Please read more about University of Turku as an employer from our Come work with us! pages. The European Commission has awarded the University of Turku the right to use the HR Excellence in Research quality label . The label is a token of the University's commitment to continuous development of the position and working conditions of researchers according to the guidelines set forth in the European Charter for Researchers. The university offers good support and orientation for international hires. Please learn more about the Finnish culture and relocation to Finland: City of Turku Welcome visitor International House of Turku Working culture: infoFinland.fi This is Finland Careers in Southwest Finland Finland - a superpower of education and innovations | University of Turku (utu.fi) The University of Turku is among the top of the world’s universities in most rankings and among the best universities in the world in certain fields. Our high-quality basic research, a multidisciplinary research profile and close cooperation in research infrastructures creates the basis for international top research. Read more about University of Turku in international university rankings. The University of Turku has several high-quality research infrastructures required for cutting-edge research. Learn more about the roadmap of research infrastructures and how the research infrastructure and expert teams offer tailored solutions for businesses and organizations . Salary and trial period The salary is determined in accordance with the university salary system for teaching and research personnel and will depend on the degree and qualifications of the applicant. For a doctoral/project researcher (OV02-OV04), the salary will be in the beginning of the employment on average 2500–2700 euros/month, depending on previous experience and skills. The amount of the salary is defined when the employment contract is prepared. A six (6) month trial period applies to the position(s). How to apply Please submit your application through our online recruitment system. The closing date for applications is 22 October  2026 at 16.00 (Europe/Helsinki). Applications should be submitted in English and they should include: A motivation letter Curriculum Vitae (CV) A list of publications (if you have) Degree certificates and academic transcripts Contact details of at least two referees (or letters of recommendation, if already available) Possible other documents that affect the decision-making (for example research plan, awards, a valid International English proficiency certificate, e.g. IELTS, TOEFL) Further information For further information about the position, please contact: ELLIS PI, Associate Professor Xucong Zhang, xucong.zhang@utu.fi . With questions about the application process, please contact: HR specialist Nina Reini, nina.reini@utu.fi . University of Turku reserves the right for justified reasons to leave the position open, to extend the application period, reopen the application process, and to consider candidates who have not submitted applications during the application period. Apply between 9 October 2026 and 22 October 2026 16:00 (Europe/Helsinki) Department of Computing The Department of Computing educates professionals for the modern digitalised society. Central themes of teaching and research include Digitalisation, Machine Learning, Autonomous and Intelligent Systems, Cybersecurity and Health Technology. The Faculty of Technology is the newest faculty of the University of Turku, it was established in the beginning of 2021. The Faculty consists of the Department of Computing, Department of Biotechnology and the Department of Mechanical and Materials Engineering. We have more than 2,500 graduate and postgraduate students and circa 600 employees, of whom more than 50 are professors. Our faculty is an international, multicultural and diverse work community. The University of Turku is an inspiring and international academic community of 25,000 students and staff in Southwest Finland. We build a sustainable future with multidisciplinary research, education, and collaboration. With us, your work will have a significant impact and relevance in the changing world. See our open vacancies Homepage LinkedIn Facebook Youtube Instagram Apply for this position English Suomi English 1-2 Doctoral Researchers in Human-Centered World Model for Human-Robot Interaction Add your picture First name Last name Email Phone Finland (Suomi) +358 Afghanistan (‫افغانستان‬‎) +93 Albania (Shqipëri) +355 Algeria (‫الجزائر‬‎) +213 American Samoa +1 Andorra +376 Angola +244 Anguilla +1 Antigua and Barbuda +1 Argentina +54 Armenia (Հայաստան) +374 Aruba +297 Ascension Island +247 Australia +61 Austria (Österreich) +43 Azerbaijan (Azərbaycan) +994 Bahamas +1 Bahrain (‫البحرين‬‎) +973 Bangladesh (বাংলাদেশ) +880 Barbados +1 Belarus (Беларусь) +375 Belgium (België) +32 Belize +501 Benin (Bénin) +229 Bermuda +1 Bhutan (འབྲུག) +975 Bolivia +591 Bosnia and Herzegovina (Босна и Херцеговина) +387 Botswana +267 Brazil (Brasil) +55 British Indian Ocean Territory +246 British Virgin Islands +1 Brunei +673 Bulgaria (България) +359 Burkina Faso +226 Burundi (Uburundi) +257 Cambodia (កម្ពុជា) +855 Cameroon (Cameroun) +237 Canada +1 Cape Verde (Kabu Verdi) +238 Caribbean Netherlands +599 Cayman Islands +1 Central African Republic (République centra