    "https://ats.talentadore.com/apply/yliopisto-opettajan-maaraaikainen-tehtava-biokuvantamisen-informatiikka-tekoalyyn-ja-koneoppimiseen-perustuva-kuva-datan-analyysi/D4vLVl?lang=en&UTUID=21701": {
      "title": "University Teacher (fixed-term position) / bioimaging informatics, artificial intelligence and machine learning based (image) data analysis",
      "description": "University Teacher (fixed-term position) / bioimaging informatics, artificial intelligence and machine learning based (image) data analysis | Institute of Biomedicine JavaScript is disabled. Please enable JavaScript for the best recruiting experience. Apply for this position University Teacher (fixed-term position) / bioimaging informatics, artificial intelligence and machine learning based (image) data analysis Institute of Biomedicine is looking for a University Teacher for a fixed term position which focuses on the following teaching areas: bioimaging informatics, artificial intelligence and machine learning based (image) data analysis. The position will be filled from 1 January 2027 onwards (or as agreed) for three years. Job description The position of a university teacher includes a wide range of teaching duties within the degree programmes in biomedical sciences, medicine and dentistry. Teaching duties and course responsibilities are primarily within undergraduate education, including our international Master’s programmes (the Master’s programme in Bioimaging and the Master’s programme in Drug Discovery and Development). Teaching duties include, amongst other things, the planning and conducting of lectures, examinations, practical assignments and online teaching. Teaching may be conducted in both Finnish and English. The role also includes supervising theses, tasks related to the organisation, planning and development of teaching, high-level research work, and university administrative duties. The successful candidate will be expected to participate actively in research in the field and to apply for research funding. Read more about studying at the Faculty of Medicine . Who we are looking for According to the qualification requirements, a person selected for the post of a university teacher is must have an applicable higher university degree good teaching skills When assessing the merits of the applicants, the following will be taken into account the teaching and research expertise within the relevant field teacher training the ability to produce study materials and multifaceted teaching recent publications in the field as well as other academic merits To succeed in this role, you will need experience of modern machine learning methods an understanding of deep neural networks programming skills, particularly in the Python programming language and relevant development environments experience of biomedical imaging an enthusiastic and innovative approach to teaching the ability to supervise international students excellent spoken and written English strong teamwork skills in a multidisciplinary and multicultural environment good organisational skills and the ability to work under pressure (time management, managing multiple tasks simultaneously) the ability to deliver multifaceted teaching and develop digital learning environments The eligibility criteria for the position must be met by the end of the application period. The following may be considered as an advantage a doctoral degree in a relevant field previous experience of publishing, teaching and supervising in the field a proven track record of securing research funding international research experience experience of high-performance computing or parallel computing environments proficiency in Finnish a vision for the direction of research in this role familiarity with the degree programmes offered by the University of Turku and the Faculty of Medicine practical experience of teaching/teaching responsibilities and research in the field of biomedicine compatibility of the candidate’s own research topics with the research priorities of the Institute of Biomedicine We value collegiality and promote equality, diversity, and inclusivity. We encourage all qualified applicants with different backgrounds to apply for our open positions. Benefits We offer you responsible and interesting tasks and the opportunity to develop your professional skills in a versatile operating environment. Please read more about University of Turku as an employer from our Come work with us! pages. The European Commission has awarded the University of Turku the right to use the HR Excellence in Research quality label . The label is a token of the University's commitment to continuous development of the position and working conditions of researchers according to the guidelines set forth in the European Charter for Researchers. The University of Turku has several high-quality research infrastructures required for cutting-edge research. Learn more about the roadmap of research infrastructures and how the research infrastructure and expert teams offer tailored solutions for businesses and organizations . The University of Turku is among the top of the world’s universities in most rankings and among the best universities in the world in certain fields. Our high-quality basic research, a multidisciplinary research profile and close cooperation in research infrastructures creates the basis for international top research. Read more about University of Turku in international university rankings. The university offers good support and orientation for international hires. Please learn more about the Finnish culture and relocation to Finland: City of Turku Welcome visitor International House of Turku Working culture: infoFinland.fi This is Finland Careers in Southwest Finland Finland - a superpower of education and innovations | University of Turku (utu.fi) Salary and trial period The salary is determined in accordance with the university salary system for teaching and research personnel (levels 4-6). In addition, a personal performance-based salary component is paid. At the beginning of the employment, the gross monthly salary is typically approximately EUR 3197-4671, depending on previous experience and expertise. The amount of the salary is defined when the employment contract is prepared. A six (6) month trial period applies to the position. How to apply Please submit your application through our online recruitment system by 4 November 2026 4 pm. Applications should include: CV ( use this template ) list of publications motivation letter teaching portfolio in accordance with the University guidelines copy of a degree certificate contact information of two referees other relevant documents Additional information For further information about the position, please contact Associate Professor Pekka Ruusuvuori, pekka.ruusuvuori@utu.fi In case you need help with the application process, please turn to HR Specialist Kristiina Nuutila, kristiina.nuutila@utu.fi, +358 50 313 5224 Apply between and Institute of Biomedicine Research at the Institute of Biomedicine is divided into three functional units: Infection and Immunity, Integrative Physiology and Pharmacology, and Cancer research. Research at our Institute includes both biomedical basic research and translational research, and the unit division expresses our research priorities. The Faculty of Medicine is a high level, international and innovative research and education unit in biomedicine, clinical medicine, dentistry and health and nursing sciences, as well as a major social contributor to health promotion, disease genesis, in the research of diagnostics and treatment and in the development of the health service and education system. The faculty provides research-based multidisciplinary undergraduate education in educational programs that educate diverse and critically minded specialists. The research is multidisciplinary and results in new information aimed at promoting the health of the population and better patient care. The University of Turku is an inspiring and international academic community of 25,000 students and staff in Southwest Finland. We build a sustainable future with multidisciplinary research, education, and collaboration. With us, your work will have a significant impact and relevance in the changing world. See our open vacancies Homepage LinkedIn Facebook Youtube Instagram Information for the applicant The application form cannot be saved as a draft. However, after submitting you can return to edit your application via the link you receive by email. The application can be edited until the application deadline. You have 6 hours to complete your application before the timeout. Instructions for submitting a job application Apply for this position English Suomi English University Teacher (fixed-term position) / bioimaging informatics, artificial intelligence and machine learning based (image) data analysis Add your picture Are you sure you want to withdraw this application? Would you like to tell us the reason for this withdrawal? Back to form Saving changes Saved!"
    },
    "https://ats.talentadore.com/apply/project-researcher-senior-researcher-for-the-development-of-research-infrastructure-for-humanoid-and-embodied-ai-turku-school-of-economics-ccr/ZvnLpO?UTUID=21711": {
      "title": "Project Researcher/Senior Researcher for the development of research infrastructure for humanoid and embodied AI, Turku School of Economics/CCR",
      "description": "Project Researcher/Senior Researcher for the development of research infrastructure for humanoid and embodied AI, Turku School of Economics/CCR | Centre for Collaborative Research JavaScript is disabled. Please enable JavaScript for the best recruiting experience. Apply for this position Project Researcher/Senior Researcher for the development of research infrastructure for humanoid and embodied AI, Turku School of Economics/CCR Turku School of Economics at the University of Turku, Finland, invites applications for a fixed-term position of Project Researcher/Senior Researcher starting as soon as possible and lasting until 31 December 2028 . The position is divided equally between developing the research infrastructure shared by Turku School of Economics and working at the Centre for Collaborative Research CCR , where the Project Researcher/Senior Researcher will be part of the Immersive Experience Lab research group. The position focuses on developing a research infrastructure based on humanoid robotics and embodied AI at Turku School of Economics, as well as conducting research using this infrastructure. The aim is to establish a long-lasting and evolving research environment for studying human–AI interaction, particularly in business research settings. The research environment built around a humanoid robot will enable experimental research on human interaction with embodied AI and the exploration of new use cases in services, customer experiences, and business. The infrastructure will be developed in collaboration with the disciplines and students of Turku School of Economics, companies, technology providers, other research infrastructures at the University of Turku, and researchers from various fields. Job description The main responsibility of the Project Researcher/Senior Researcher is to develop the research infrastructure built around a humanoid robot and its use in research. The work involves continuously developing the technical and operational infrastructure, introducing new solutions and functionalities, and designing and conducting research studies and experiments in collaboration with researchers. The Project Researcher/Senior Researcher will participate in research projects in which the humanoid and embodied AI infrastructure and its development play a central role. The position involves planning and conducting research, publishing scientific findings, and preparing new research projects and applications for external funding, with a specific focus on the humanoid robot and its associated research infrastructure. The work requires the ability to connect research questions with the opportunities and limitations of technology and to describe technical solutions in research plans and funding applications. The duties also include the practical coordination and development of the research infrastructure: providing guidance and training to users, developing operating principles for the humanoid robot, carrying out tasks related to safe operation, communicating about the infrastructure, and resolving problems. The Project Researcher/Senior Researcher will serve as a contact person for technology providers and must be able to discuss solutions related to AI technology, robotics, and embodied interaction with both technical experts and technology researchers. The work involves extensive collaboration with the different disciplines and students of Turku School of Economics, for example to enable the use of the infrastructure in research, theses, teaching, and projects. The position also includes collaboration with companies to develop new use cases, research services, and pilots, as well as collaboration with other research infrastructures at the University of Turku. All CCR employees also actively contribute to the development of the unit’s activities. The nature of the position requires on-site work at Turku School of Economics; the amount and arrangements of on-site work will be agreed flexibly with the selected candidate. Who we are looking for A project researcher is required to have a higher university degree suitable for the position. When assessing the merits of the applicants, special emphasis will place on competence and practical expertise in the field in question. A senior researcher is required to have a doctoral degree suitable for the position and the ability to conduct independent scientific research. Evidence of academic research work is required. The qualification requirements for the positions are defined in the University of Turku Rules of Procedure . We expect you to have: Evidence of scientific research and publication experience Readiness to understand research infrastructure that uses AI technology, robotics, and other interactive technologies Ability to communicate with technology providers, technical experts, and technology researchers Ability to design and prepare research settings that make use of emerging technologies Good collaboration, communication, and organisational skills, as well as the ability to work independently and proactively Ability to collaborate with students, researchers, companies, and other stakeholders Excellent spoken and written English skills; proficiency in Finnish is considered an advantage The following will be considered an advantage: Research or professional experience, or alternatively strong insight, in one or more of the following areas: humanoid robotics, embodied AI, human–robot interaction, human–computer interaction, human–AI interaction, generative AI, or interactive technologies Technical understanding of, for example, large language models (LLMs), sensors, robotics, software development, programming, system integrations, or research equipment Experience in developing research environments or infrastructures and building technology-based research settings Experience in interdisciplinary research projects, business research, preparing research funding applications, industry collaboration, or working with technology providers Experience in collaborating with students, teaching, supervising theses, or communicating research and development activities to different audiences We welcome applicants who already have experience in the field, as well as those seeking to develop their careers in this area. We value collegiality and promote equality, diversity, and inclusivity. We encourage all qualified applicants with different backgrounds to apply for our open positions. What we offer The position is based at Turku School of Economics, University of Turku, and in the Immersive Experience Lab research group at the Centre for Collaborative Research CCR . It offers a unique opportunity to build new research capabilities based on humanoid robotics and embodied AI technology and to combine technological development, scientific research, collaboration with students, and industry collaboration. We offer you responsible and interesting tasks and the opportunity to develop your professional skills in a versatile operating environment. You get a professional and inspiring team to support your work. We take care of your well-being at work and the functionality of your everyday life, e.g. with the help of flexible working hours and our well-being services. Please read more about University of Turku as an employer from our Come work with us! pages. The European Commission has awarded the University of Turku the right to use the HR Excellence in Research quality label . The label is a token of the University's commitment to continuous development of the position and working conditions of researchers according to the guidelines set forth in the European Charter for Researchers. The university offers good support and orientation for international hires. Please learn more about the Finnish culture and relocation to Finland: City of Turku Welcome visitor International House of Turku Working culture: infoFinland.fi This is Finland Careers in Southwest Finland Finland - a superpower of education and innovations | University of Turku (utu.fi) The University of Turku is among the top of the world’s universities in most rankings and among the best universities in the world in certain fields. Our high-quality basic research, a multidisciplinary research profile and close cooperation in research infrastructures creates the basis for international top research. Read more about University of Turku in international university rankings. Salary and trial period The salary for the post is determined in accordance with the university salary system for teaching and research personnel. The salary for a Project Research (OV3-OV4) in the beginning of employment is approximately 2900-3400 EUR per month depending on previous experience and competence. The salary for a Senior Researcher (OV5-OV6) in the beginning of employment is approximately 3800 – 4600 EUR per month depending on previous experience and competence. The position has a trial period of six months. How to apply Please submit your application through our online recruitment system. The closing date for applications is 11.11.2026 at 16.00 (Europe/Helsinki) . Applicants should enclose with their application: motivation letter CV according to the TENK model list of publications degree certificate(s) other documents that may influence the filling of the position Further information For further information about the position, please contact: Research Director Jukka Vahlo, tel. +358 50 911 9776 or jukka.vahlo(at)utu.fi or Director Antti Saurama, puh. 040 592 4921, antti.saurama(at)utu.fi. With questions about the application process, please contact: HR Specialist Mira Liikkanen, tel. +358 50 400 2721 or mira.liikkanen(at)utu.fi. Apply between and Centre for Collaborative Research The Centre for Collaborative Research CRR focuses on research work with other organisations in a cooperative way. We study business transformations at different levels: individuals, businesses, industries and in society as a whole. Besides research we develop and create prerequisites for industry-academia collaboration and innovation activities for our faculty at Turku School of Economics. We’re inspired by collaboration, transparency and impact. Turku School of Economics is known for impactful research, inspiring learning experiences, future-oriented thinking, and versatile collaboration with stakeholders. As a recognition of excellence in business education and research, TSE has been rewarded international AACSB-accreditation, read more . The University of Turku is an inspiring and international academic community of 25,000 students and staff in Southwest Finland. We build a sustainable future with multidisciplinary research, education, and collaboration. With us, your work will have a significant impact and relevance in the changing world. See our open vacancies Homepage LinkedIn Facebook Youtube Instagram Apply for this position English Suomi English Project Researcher/Senior Researcher for the development of research infrastructure for humanoid and embodied AI, Turku School of Economics/CCR Add your picture Are you sure you want to withdraw this application? Would you like to tell us the reason for this withdrawal? Back to form Saving changes Saved!"
    },
    "https://ats.talentadore.com/apply/erikoistutkija/m5nOR1?lang=en&UTUID=21705": {
      "title": "Senior researcher",
      "description": "Senior researcher | INVEST Research Flagship Centre JavaScript is disabled. Please enable JavaScript for the best recruiting experience. Apply for this position Senior researcher The Faculty of Social Sciences, INVEST Flagship and Research Centre at the University of Turku invites applications for a contract-based, fixed term, part time 80% position of a Project Researcher or Senior Researcher (post-doctoral position) from 1.1.2027 to 31.12.2029. Employment starts on 1.1.2027 or as agreed. The recruited researcher will work in the RCoF-funded HIPES project (under the INVEST Flagship). The HIPES project: Testing a Hypothesis of Inflated Prevalence of mental health problems, while Expanding it with a Social Lens Over the past decades, extensive efforts (e.g., campaigns) have been made to improve public understanding and awareness of mental health problems. Paradoxically, over the same period, reported rates of mental health problems – especially anxiety and depression – have risen dramatically among young people. The prevalence inflation hypothesis suggests that awareness efforts may not only have improved recognition of existing problems but also, for some youth, led to overinterpretation of mild symptoms as disorders – thus inflating the prevalence estimates. Overinterpretation can be problematic, as it may trigger self-fulfilling prophecies and thus, worsen symptoms over time. The prevalence inflation hypothesis remains untested to date and overlooks the influence of adolescents’ proximal environments – school, peers, and parents. HIPES will collect various types of data (surveys, daily diaries, experiments, and interviews) to test how these proximal contexts shape adolescents’ accurate recognition versus overinterpretation, and how social interactions mediate the effects of overinterpretation on the aggravation of mental health problems. Job description This project is situated within the INVEST Psychology research group (led by prof. Christina Salmivalli), see https://invest.utu.fi/psychology/. We are seeking an applicant with strong motivation to plan and conduct high quality research (including designing studies, publishing papers, applying for grants, presenting at conferences), as well as skills for teamwork and collaboration. Who we are looking for Requirements According to the University of Turku rules of procedure, section 36: A person selected for the post of senior research fellow is required to have a doctoral degree and the ability to do independent scientific work. For the post of a senior research fellow on the third step of the teaching and research staff career structure, evidence of scientific research work and the necessary teaching skills are also required. For the post of a senior researcher on the second step of the teaching and research staff career structure, an individual with a higher university degree and especially strong practical expertise in the field in question can also be appointed. According to section 37 a person selected for the post of project researcher is required to have a higher university degree. When assessing the merits of the applicants, special emphasis will be placed on competence and practical expertise in the field in question. Successful performance in the position requires: a) a doctoral degree in psychology or a related field. Those expected to acquire such a degree within six months are also eligible to apply. b) ability to conduct independent research and experience with publishing in peer-reviewed journals c) advanced skills in quantitative methods d) excellent scientific writing skills in English The eligibility requirements for the position must be fulfilled by the end of the application period for the position. Desirable qualifications Knowledge and previous experience in conducting research on the specific topics related HIPES: mental health problems, adolescence, peers, parents, self-labelling, coping Experience with relevant methodology for the projects: longitudinal survey studies, daily diaries, social network analyses, and/or designing experiments Finnish language skills are considered an asset We value collegiality and promote equality, diversity, and inclusivity. We encourage all qualified applicants with different backgrounds to apply for our open positions. Benefits We offer you responsible and interesting tasks and the opportunity to develop your professional skills in a versatile operating environment. You get a professional and inspiring team to support your work. We take care of your well-being at work and the functionality of your everyday life, e.g. with the help of flexible working hours and our well-being services. Possibilities to develop your expertise – We encourage our personnel to develop their professional expertise by offering versatile training and competence development possibilities which employees can take advantage of during their working hours. Also, the course offering of Open University is free of charge for our personnel. Your well-being is important to us! – In addition to comprehensive occupational health care, our own well-being services monitor, support and develop the well-being of our personnel. You are entitled to use the CampusSport’s services at a personnel price. We support your work-life balance – Flexible working hours and extensive remote work options help you balance work and leisure time. An inspiring and supportive work community – We encourage each other and value working together! Please read more about University of Turku as an employer from our Come work with us! pages. The European Commission has awarded the University of Turku the right to use the HR Excellence in Research quality label . The label is a token of the University's commitment to continuous development of the position and working conditions of researchers according to the guidelines set forth in the European Charter for Researchers. The university offers good support and orientation for international hires. Please learn more about the Finnish culture and relocation to Finland: City of Turku Welcome visitor International House of Turku Working culture: infoFinland.fi This is Finland Careers in Southwest Finland Finland - a superpower of education and innovations | University of Turku (utu.fi) Salary and trial period The salary is determined in accordance with the university salary system for teaching and research personnel. The job requirement level for the Senior Researcher position is OV05-OV06, while the job requirement level for the Project Researcher position is OV02-OV04. In addition, a personal performance-based salary component will be paid. Depending on the successful candidate's previous experience and expertise, the monthly salary at the start of the employment will be approximately €3000-3700 for a Senior Researcher and €2100-2700 for a Project Researcher. The position has a trial period of six months. How to apply Please submit your application through our online recruitment system. The closing date for applications is 13.11.2026 at 16.00 (Europe/Helsinki) . Please write your application and accompanying documents in English. Applicants must enclose with their application: a motivation letter ( max 2 pages) in which the applicant describes their research interests and how their research interests relate to the HIPES project as well as the larger research group a CV (max 2 pages) a list of publications (with brief description of the applicant’s role in each publication) a “job market paper” (a published article or a manuscript) that best describes the applicant’s qualifications for the position and how she or he has contributed to the scientific literature copy or copies of diplomas (if the degree / degrees have not been completed at the University of Turku For those in the process of defending their thesis, a statement from the supervisor regarding the estimated date of the dissertation defense Letters of recommendation (with contact information) for the applicant from two prior academic supervisors or persons acquainted with the applicant and their work Further information For further information about the position, please contact: Academy research fellow Lydia Wijnen, lalawi@utu.fi With questions about the application process, please contact: HR specialist Laura Nieminen, laura.nieminen@utu.fi , +35829 450 4987 Apply between and INVEST Research Flagship Centre Think, Question, Get Inspired – New Welfare State The research flagship Inequalities, Interventions, and New Welfare State ( INVEST ) aims at providing a new model for the welfare state that is more equal, better targeted to problem groups, more anticipatory as well as economically and socially sustainable. The existing research indicates that the Nordic welfare states are efficient in reducing the negative outcomes that are related to many of the structural family disadvantages, such as parental low education, unemployment or poverty. Despite this, children and youth are still particularly vulnerable when negative life course events take place unexpectedly or when many disadvantages accumulate to the same families. The growth environments can strengthen these negative effects. The flagship has been funded by the Academy of Finland and is implemented in cooperation with the University of Turku and the Institute of Health and Welfare (THL). The multidisciplinary project combines sociology, social policy, demography, psychology and psychiatry, in addition to the other connected fields of sciences. The University of Turku is an inspiring and international academic community of 25,000 students and staff in Southwest Finland. We build a sustainable future with multidisciplinary research, education, and collaboration. With us, your work will have a significant impact and relevance in the changing world. See our open vacancies Homepage LinkedIn Facebook Youtube Instagram Information for the applicant The application form cannot be saved as a draft. However, after submitting you can return to edit your application via the link you receive by email. The application can be edited until the application deadline. You have 6 hours to complete your application before the timeout. Instructions for submitting a job application Apply for this position English Suomi English Senior researcher Add your picture Are you sure you want to withdraw this application? Would you like to tell us the reason for this withdrawal? Back to form Saving changes Saved!"
    },
    "https://ats.talentadore.com/apply/doctoral-researcher-in-applied-cryptography/Zy1dpA?UTUID=21713": {
      "title": "Doctoral Researcher in Applied Cryptography",
      "description": "Doctoral Researcher in Applied Cryptography | Department of Computing JavaScript is disabled. Please enable JavaScript for the best recruiting experience. Apply for this position Doctoral Researcher in Applied Cryptography The Department of Computing at the Faculty of Technology invites applications for a full-time, salaried Doctoral Researcher position. This role focuses on the applied cryptography and privacy enhancing technologies research. The fixed-term position starts based on mutual agreement and ends on 30.9.2029. Job description This position is integrated into a high-impact European research project. As a Doctoral researcher, you will conduct deep-dive research into the applied cryptography domain. You will join an elite, interdisciplinary team, collaborating closely with leading academic experts and industrial architects across Europe. The successful candidate will focus on one of following pillars: Privacy enhancing technologies: Database security and privacy, designing theoretical protocols and algorithms. Post-quantum cryptography: Developing robust mechanisms for data protection and user privacy, focusing on either signature or encryption. Responsibilities Design, develop, and implement state-of-the-art PETs and post-quantum cryptographic schemes. Collaborate closely with top-tier European universities and industrial partners. Participate in project implementation and dissemination activities. Contribute to academic life by supervising MSc and Bachelor students, and assisting in teaching activities. Engage in training opportunities including proposal writing, high-impact scientific publishing, and collaborative research with international teams. Who we are looking for Requirements MSc degree in Computer Science, Mathematics, or related field. A solid foundation in Computer Science with a deep understanding of PETs and cryptographic related algorithms. A strong interest in or prior experience with cryptography. Excellent analytical and problem-solving skills. Interest in collaborative research with both academia and industry. Good English proficiency (written and spoken). Qualification requirements The eligibility criteria for prospective applicants are defined in the University of Turku’s rules of procedure . A person selected for the post of doctoral researcher is required to have a right to pursue a doctoral degree at the University of Turku. In addition, when acquiring their degree or otherwise, they are required to have demonstrated the ability to undertake postgraduate studies and the capacity to complete a doctoral degree in accordance with the research plan. Please note that before obtaining the study right for a Doctoral Program, the job title will be Project Researcher , and the duration of the contract will be made until 31.7.2027 at the latest. The candidate is expected to apply for the study right in the next available call to e.g. the Doctoral Programme in Technology. Thus, please check the student information and application criteria Doctoral Programme in Technology - Admission Criteria and Instructions for Applicants | University of Turku (please pay attention to the mandatory skill level in English). Read more about the University of Turku's doctoral programmes and how to apply for study rights Join us for your doctoral studies at the University of Turku! | University of Turku In exceptional cases, we may also consider applicants who have completed nearly all the studies required for a master's degree in a relevant field. In such cases, the job title at the start of the employment will be Research Assistant and the starting salary (OV1) is on average 2400 euros/month, depending on competence and experience. We value collegiality and promote equality, diversity, and inclusivity. We encourage all qualified applicants with different backgrounds to apply for our open positions. Benefits We Offer: A fully funded PhD position in an internationally recognized research environment. Opportunities to publish in top-tier cybersecurity journals and flag-ship conferences. Opportunities to collaborate with and visit outstanding European universities and industrial partners. Training courses for academic researchers, e.g., proposal writing, scientific writing, project development, teaching qualification. A vibrant, international, and supportive research community. We offer you responsible and interesting tasks and the opportunity to develop your professional skills in a versatile operating environment. You get a professional and inspiring team to support your work. We take care of your well-being at work and the functionality of your everyday life, e.g. with the help of flexible working hours and our well-being services. Please read more about University of Turku as an employer from our Come work with us! pages. The European Commission has awarded the University of Turku the right to use the HR Excellence in Research quality label . The label is a token of the University's commitment to continuous development of the position and working conditions of researchers according to the guidelines set forth in the European Charter for Researchers. The university offers good support and orientation for international hires. Please learn more about the Finnish culture and relocation to Finland: City of Turku Welcome visitor International House of Turku Working culture: infoFinland.fi This is Finland Careers in Southwest Finland Finland - a superpower of education and innovations | University of Turku (utu.fi) The University of Turku is among the top of the world’s universities in most rankings and among the best universities in the world in certain fields. Our high-quality basic research, a multidisciplinary research profile and close cooperation in research infrastructures creates the basis for international top research. Read more about University of Turku in international university rankings. The University of Turku has several high-quality research infrastructures required for cutting-edge research. Learn more about the roadmap of research infrastructures and how the research infrastructure and expert teams offer tailored solutions for businesses and organizations . Salary and trial period The salary is determined in accordance with the university salary system for teaching and research personnel and will depend on the degree and qualifications of the applicant. For a doctoral/project researcher (OV02-OV04), the salary will be at the beginning of employment on average 2500–2700 euros/month, depending on previous experience and skills. The amount of the salary is defined when the employment contract is prepared. A six (6) month trial period applies to the position. How to apply Please submit your application through our online recruitment system. The closing date for applications is 4 December 2026 at 16.00 (Europe/Helsinki). Your application must include the followings: A motivation letter (Please specify your research interests, 1 page is sufficient) Curriculum Vitae (CV) A list of publications Copies of Bachelor and MSc degree certificates with translation in English or in Finnish Proof of Language Proficiency, e.g. IELTS or TOEFL, or other certified international tests. Other documents that may affect the decision-making (for example a research plan, awards) Further information Home page of the research group: http://www.utu.fi/cyber For further information about the position, please contact: Associate Professor Kaitai Liang, kaitai.liang@utu.fi . With questions about the application process, please contact: HR Specialist Nina Reini, nina.reini@utu.fi . Apply between and Department of Computing The Department of Computing educates professionals for the modern digitalised society. Central themes of teaching and research include Digitalisation, Machine Learning, Autonomous and Intelligent Systems, Cybersecurity and Health Technology. The Faculty of Technology is the newest faculty of the University of Turku, it was established in the beginning of 2021. The Faculty consists of the Department of Computing, Department of Biotechnology and the Department of Mechanical and Materials Engineering. We have more than 2,500 graduate and postgraduate students and circa 600 employees, of whom more than 50 are professors. Our faculty is an international, multicultural and diverse work community. The University of Turku is an inspiring and international academic community of 25,000 students and staff in Southwest Finland. We build a sustainable future with multidisciplinary research, education, and collaboration. With us, your work will have a significant impact and relevance in the changing world. See our open vacancies Homepage LinkedIn Facebook Youtube Instagram Apply for this position English Suomi English Doctoral Researcher in Applied Cryptography Add your picture Are you sure you want to withdraw this application? Would you like to tell us the reason for this withdrawal? Back to form Saving changes Saved!"
    },
    "https://ats.talentadore.com/apply/doctoral-researcher-or-project-researcher-educational-psychology-or-learning-analytics/Dw14pG?UTUID=21721": {
      "title": "Doctoral researcher or Project Researcher, Educational Psychology or Learning Analytics",
      "description": "Doctoral researcher or Project Researcher, Educational Psychology or Learning Analytics  | Turku Research Institute for Learning Analytics JavaScript is disabled. Please enable JavaScript for the best recruiting experience. Apply for this position Doctoral researcher or Project Researcher, Educational Psychology or Learning Analytics Turku Research Institute for Learning Analytics (TRILA) is currently seeking to recruit a doctoral researcher / a project researcher . The fixed term position starts on the 1st of January 2027 or upon mutual agreement, and lasts two years at the most. In the case the selected candidate does not yet have the right to study for a doctoral degree at the University of Turku, the title of Project Researcher will be used at first, and the study right for a doctoral degree should be applied in the next possible call (during 2027): University of Turku Graduate School (UTUGS) and Doctoral Programs . Job describtion The vacancy is a part of the Academy Project “Teachers and digital environments: Interrelations between teachers’ motivation, wellbeing and children’s learning project (1.9.2026-1.8.2030)”, funded by the Research Council of Finland (PI Silinskas). The position will focus on either of the following research themes / objectives: Teachers’ psychological functioning (e.g., well-being, motivation), digital beliefs/practices and their associations to children’s achievement and motivation. Technological/digital aspects of teaching and learning. For example, the digital trace data and the psychological and educational aspects and learning strategies they may reflect (e.g., rehearsal, task persistence, inaccuracy, spontaneity). The duties of the doctoral researcher include conducting his/her own doctoral research and completing doctoral courses. Qualifications we are looking for •  The candidates must hold a master degree in a field relevant to the research topics (Psychology, Education, Cognitive Science, Learning Analytics, Linguistics, Social Sciences, Computer Science / Information Technology, Mathematics and Statistics, or in a other relevant field) or will graduate soon. Additionally, applicants must have completed a higher education degree or otherwise demonstrated the ability to pursue postgraduate studies and complete a doctoral degree according to the research plan. • Previous experience in managing data and statistical analysis methods (e.g., multilevel modelling, using SPSS or Mplus statistical programs) is an advantage. • Experience in research/development work related to educational psychology and digital learning environments is an advantage. • The candidates are expected to have good English skills. The qualification requirements of the position state in the University of Turku’s Rules of Procedure: https://www.utu.fi/en/university/organisation . The eligibility requirements for doctoral researchers are specified in the University of Turku's regulations ( How to Apply for Doctoral Training | University of Turku ). In the case the selected candidate does not yet have the right to study for a doctoral degree at the University of Turku, the title of Project Researcher will used at first, and the study right for a doctoral degree should be applied in the next possible call (spring 2027): University of Turku Graduate School (UTUGS) and Doctoral Programs. If the candidate is close to graduation (MSc or equivalent), an employment contract is initially made under the title of a research assistant and the right to study for a doctoral degree is applied for after graduation in the next possible call (in a year 2027). We primarily seek to recruit Doctoral Researcher / Project Researcher . However, in well justified cases, applicants who have completed almost all master studies required for a master in a relevant field may also be considered. In such cases, the job title at the start of the employment will be Research Assistant and salary will be in the beginning on average 2 300 –2 450 euros/month, depending on previous experience and skills. A person selected for the post of Researcher assistant is required to have a copy of transcript of study records, which must be attached as an annex to the application. When assessing the merits of the applicants, special emphasis will be placed on competence and practical expertise in the field in question. The doctoral researcher position requires residence in Finland. Work language is English. Our workplace values equality and diversity, and therefore, we encourage qualified applicants from all backgrounds to apply for our open position. The doctoral researcher position requires residence in Finland. Work language is English. Our workplace values equality and diversity, and therefore, we encourage qualified applicants from all backgrounds to apply for our open position. We offer We offer you responsible and interesting tasks and the opportunity to develop your skills in a dynamic and international environment. You will be supported by a professional and inspiring team and a group of experienced supervisors. In your work, you will become part of a wide network of doctoral researchers, researchers, and supervisors within the TRILA and EDUCA Flagship Project. We care about your well-being and the functionality of your everyday life through flexible working hours and our well-being services. Please read more about University of Turku as an employee from our Come work with us! pages. The university offers good support and orientation for international hires. Please learn more about the Finnish culture and relocation to Finland: • City of Turku , • Welcome visitor , • Career in Southwest Finland , • International House of Turku • Working culture: infoFinland.fi • This is Finland • Careers in Southwest Finland • Finland - a superpower of education and innovations | University of Turku (utu.fi) Read more about us on the website Come Work with Us! , where you can find additional information about what the university offers its employees. The European Commission has granted the University of Turku the right to use the HR Excellence in Research logo as a sign of the university's commitment to continuously improving the status and working conditions of researchers in line with the goals of the European Charter for Researchers. Salary and Trial Period Salary will be determined in a contract. Salary will be determined through University of Turku system for research and teaching personnel and for a doctoral researcher / project researcher will be in levels 2-4 and personal performance will be added to task-specific salary. The salary will commensurate with qualifications and experience and basis on the University salary system and will in the beginning of the employment be approximately 2 550 –3 200 € / month. A six (6) months trial period applies to the position. How to apply Applicants are kindly asked to submit their applications using the online application form by November 30, 2026, at 4:00 p.m. local time in Finland (Europe/Helsinki) . Applications sent via email are not considered. The application link can be found on the university's website at the beginning of the advertisement (\" Apply for this job \"). The application documents that should be included in English and in PDF format (note that the application form does not specify the attachments): A short and free-form motivation/cover letter (max 2 pages), including your research interests, previous experience and merits in relation to the qualifications for this position Curriculum vitae List of publications Copy of Master degree certificate with an official translation in English, in Finnish or in Swedish Names and contact information of 1–3 referees Any other documents relevant to fulfilling the requirements of the position: Prerequisites for admission and Proof of language skills see How to Apply for Doctoral Training (see before applying -section:) Candidates selected for the interviews will be interviewed in December 2026. Decisions regarding doctoral researcher will be made in December, 2026. For Further Information For more information about the position, please contact Senior Research Fellow Gintas Silinskas ( gintautas.silinskas@utu.fi ) If you have any questions about the application process, please contact HR Specialist Susanna Virtanen ( susanna.virtanen@utu.fi ). Edited October 29: The end date of the call for applications has postponed and a new end date will be on the 30th of November. and the interview schedules will be aligned with this new deadline. Apply between and Turku Research Institute for Learning Analytics The TRILA is a research group at the University of Turku's Faculty of Mathematics and Natural Sciences, focusing on digital teaching and learning analytics. The group supports the strategy of the University of Turku by developing the quality of teaching and promoting digital education and the spread of the learning analytics ecosystem in Finland and abroad. Most Finnish primary schools use the ViLLE system developed by the TRILA group. In the Faculty of Science , we seek the truth and develop solutions for sustainable future and intelligent society. Science Fiction becomes reality. The University of Turku is an inspiring and international academic community of 25,000 students and staff in Southwest Finland. We build a sustainable future with multidisciplinary research, education, and collaboration. With us, your work will have a significant impact and relevance in the changing world. See our open vacancies Homepage LinkedIn Facebook Youtube Instagram Information for the applicant The application form cannot be saved as a draft. However, after submitting you can return to edit your application via the link you receive by email. The application can be edited until the application deadline. You have 6 hours to complete your application before the timeout. Instructions for submitting a job application Apply for this position Doctoral researcher or 